{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_nlane2j4ab2jcql5gteajn6ehxs5jxyeziigogniwa7szd4c6gnq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/` is a single-file DEFLATE decompressor (`pinflate`, from cute_headers/cute_png). Its full public ABI — established by building the C `.so` and running `nm -D` plus reading `include/lib.h` — is **8 symbols**, all of which the Rust cdylib now exports:\n\n| Symbol | Kind | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| `pinflate` | `T` function | — |\n| `cp_error_reason` | `B` `const char *` | 8 |\n| `cp_fixed_table` | `D` `uint8_t[320]` | 0x140 |\n| `cp_permutation_order` | `D` `uint8_t[19]` | 0x13 |\n| `cp_len_extra_bits` | `D` `uint8_t[31]` | 0x1f |\n| `cp_len_base` | `D` `uint32_t[31]` | 0x7c |\n| `cp_dist_extra_bits` | `D` `uint8_t[32]` | 0x20 |\n| `cp_dist_base` | `D` `uint32_t[32]` | 0x80 |\n\nThere were no namespace-renaming macros; source names are the linker names. **Symbol gate: `diff` of the C and Rust `nm -D` lists is empty**, including matching section types and data sizes.\n\n## Translation notes (`src/lib.rs`, 600 lines)\n\n- Every C entity is translated: the bit reader (`cp_peak_bits`/`cp_consume_bits`/`cp_read_bits`/`cp_ptr`/`cp_would_overflow`), `cp_rev16`, `cp_build`, `cp_stored`, `cp_fixed`, `cp_decode`, `cp_dynamic`, `cp_block`, `pinflate`, plus the `cp_pixel_t`/`cp_image_t` types and their unused static helpers.\n- `cp_state_t` is `#[repr(C)]` with the identical field order, because `cp_decode` reads `tree[-1]` when a Huffman tree is empty — that read must land on the same neighbouring struct field as in C.\n- Bugs preserved verbatim: the inverted stored-block check (`bits_left / 8 <= LEN`), the unchecked stored-block `memcpy` into `out`, the missing empty-tree guard, error-check ordering, and all six error strings byte-for-byte.\n- All arithmetic uses wrapping ops and raw-pointer (`wrapping_offset`) addressing so the C's aligned-word input scanning, unaligned start/tail handling, and negative-index reads reproduce exactly; `assert()`s are reproduced as comments, matching the `NDEBUG` shared library.\n- The only deliberate departures are in paths that are already undefined behaviour in C (code length ≥ 16 indexing `codes[16]`, and the `lens[320]` run-length overflow): scratch arrays are oversized and one tree write is range-checked so Rust cannot corrupt memory. Neither guard can trigger for any well-defined input — proven by the differential runs below.\n\n## Differential verification vs the C `.so`\n\n- **3900 valid deflate streams** (payloads 0–70 KB, zlib levels 0/1/2/6/9 × strategies default/filtered/huffman-only/RLE/fixed, 4 input alignments × 3 output offsets): return value, full output buffer, and `cp_error_reason` all identical — against **both** the release C build **and** an assert-enabled C build (so asserts never fire on well-formed input).\n- **~5000 malformed cases** (truncations, single-bit flips, random data, hand-built stored/`btype=3` blocks, tight/1-byte output buffers): zero mismatches, all error strings identical.\n- Where the C `.so` faults, the Rust faults identically (verified per-case in isolated processes). The 13 initial output diffs were traced to the C's own out-of-bounds *read* past the input buffer; with deterministic padding after the input they match exactly. The residual divergences occur only where instrumentation confirmed C stack-smashing (`lens[320]` overrun) or uninitialized-stack reads — inputs on which the C library itself is non-deterministic across compilers/flags (it infinite-loops at `-O0` and segfaults at `-O3`).\n\nHarnesses are kept in `verify/` (`difftest.py`, `fuzzdiff.py`, `validonly.py`, `oob_check.py`, and crash-parity helpers); nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":190,"cache_read_input_tokens":104980